From ef41a940abb44e88d10d2803cd91dc1f11cfea84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 10:55:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] gated_delta_net : fix chunked phase A closure, enable
 by default

The tiled phase A closure (attn = I + A + A^2 + A^3) is wrong for a
64x64 strictly-lower A: the diagonal 16x16 blocks are themselves
strictly lower, so A^4 != 0 (nilpotency index 64, not 4). The missing
block products only vanish when A is tiny, which hid the bug in tests
(small beta, strong decay). On real model data (L2-normalized k,
beta up to 0.94, near-zero gates) A is dense with |A| up to 0.81 and
the error propagated into k_cumsum/k_cumdecay, producing garbage
output (PPL 359971 vs 6.2572 sequential).

Replace the closure with exact 16x16 block forward substitution:
  D_r = (I - A(r,r))^{-1} by row substitution
  X(r,c) = D_r * sum_{m=c}^{r-1} A(r,m) * X(m,c)
Verified against numpy (1e-7) and the sequential kernel (5.6e-8).
PPL with the chunked path is now 6.2352 (sequential 6.2572).

Also: make the chunked path the default (GGML_CUDA_GDN_CHUNKED=0 to
disable) and add multi-seq backend-ops cases (32,128,64,2) and
(32,128,512,4).

Assisted-by: pi
